WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.749 --> 00:00:04.000
Hi everyone, my name is Sai Vennam with the IBM Cloud team.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.210
Today the topic on everyone's mind: IBM and Red Hat.

00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:10.280
Now our philosophy is straightforward:

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.740
Red Hat works, so let's keep it that way.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:15.200
This includes preserving their independence,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.610
their culture, as well as their commitment to open source.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:20.900
Now we're in a very unique position here,

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.260
we're seeing rapid growth of applications being developed on the cloud

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:27.160
but that's linked with increasing complexity.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:32.280
The next chapter of cloud computing is going to demand flexibility and choice.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.600
That choice starts from the ground up

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.580
when choosing the environments to run or modernize your applications.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.000
So, you can choose public or private clouds,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.540
or even on-premise environments.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.940
Building on that, we have the platform layer

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.280
which is supported by Red Hat's open source technologies.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.800
So, we have Red Hat Enterprise Linux,

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:54.920
as well as OpenShift.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.280
Now this is powered by open source technology, Kubernetes.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:06.260
So, coming back to choice, if we wanted to use native Kubernete over OpenShift, that's also an option.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:09.460
Building on that, we have the capabilities
layer.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.900
This is what developers need to develop engaging new applications.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:16.900
This would include things like databases,

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:20.100
maybe their favorite DevOps tool chains,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.240
or even their middleware platforms.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:25.500
So, for example,

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:28.480
we know that, for running J2EE applications,

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:31.960
developers may choose JBoss or WebSphere Liberty.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.650
Regardless of whether or not you choose Red Hat or IBM technologies,

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.369
we will continue to support both fully as
we move forward.

00:01:40.369 --> 00:01:46.080
Finally, all of this is channeling our users
to create new or engaging applications

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.680
by taking advantage of higher value services.

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:50.890
This is where IBM truly shines.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:55.840
So, these include AI and machine learning capabilities.

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:01.340
To summarize, from the ground up we have a hybrid multicloud platform

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.640
where you can innovate anywhere.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:09.200
We have open source technologies that Red Hat provides like OpenShift and Red Hat Enterprise Linux.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:12.120
All together with their suite of technologies.

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:16.140
That, combined with IBM's commitment and expertise with enterprise

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.300
as well as our own suite of technologies,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.020
is opening new doors to hybrid cloud that we've never seen before.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:26.320
At the end of the day, it all comes down to an idea.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.280
An idea that you build out into an application.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.720
An application built on industry best practices that follow security guidelines and compliances.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:40.540
Because we want the same thing that you do, and that is happy users.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:45.480
Thanks for joining me for this quick overview of Red Hat and IBM synergy.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.780
If you like this video, or have any comments, be sure to drop a "like" or comment below.

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:53.500
And if you want to see more videos like this in the future, please subscribe.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:54.460
Thank you.

